# The build context filter, and half of the leak boundary.
#
# The name matters. `Dockerfile.dockerignore` is honoured ONLY by BuildKit; the
# legacy builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0, or any Docker before 23) ignores it
# entirely and every held-out row enters the context. `.dockerignore` is
# honoured by both, so this file has the name that cannot be switched off.
#
# The other half is the Dockerfile's explicit COPY list: it never copies the
# context wholesale, so held-out data does not reach the image even where a
# filter is not applied. Both halves are deliberate — one of them being
# builder-dependent is exactly why there are two.
state/corpus/val
state/corpus/test
state/baseline_val.json
state/baseline_test.json
state/cache
state/candidates
state/staged
state/runs
outputs
.venv
